# SQL Result Explainer: settings for the language model
#
# Prerequisites
#   1. Python 3.10 or newer
#   2. An OpenRouter API key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
#      A full run of all ten questions costs well under one US cent.
#
# Setup: copy this file to .env and paste your key below.
# .env is gitignored. Never commit a real key.
#
# Without a key everything still works: explanations come from the built-in,
# deterministic template instead of a model.

LLM_API_KEY=

# Models are chosen automatically, so there is nothing to pick:
#   google/gemini-4-argon   writes every first answer (grounded on every question in
#                           evaluation, never slower than 14 seconds)
#   z-ai/glm-5.3            second opinion, only when that answer fails the grounding
#                           checks or the first model is down or too slow
# See docs/model-evaluation.md for the comparison behind this choice.

# Optional overrides, e.g. to run fully local with Ollama (no key needed):
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_DRAFT_MODEL=llama3.2
# LLM_RETRY_MODEL=llama3.2
# LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=45            # deadline per answer, start to finish
